# boichard_fig1.ped -- PUBLISHED WORKED EXAMPLE, transcribed with provenance.
#
# SOURCE: Boichard D, Maignel L, Verrier E (1997) "The value of using
#         probabilities of gene origin to measure genetic variability in a
#         population." Genet Sel Evol 29:5-23.
#         FIGURE 1 and TABLE I, article page 9.
#         (HAL scan hal-00894153; PDF page 6 = article page 9.)
#
# Animals 1-8 carry the paper's own numbering, so this file can be read
# directly against Table I. Animals 9-13 are the five unnumbered circles the
# figure draws inside the "Population under study" ellipse; the paper gives
# them no labels, so they are numbered here in drawing order (left to right).
#
# TOPOLOGY, read from the figure. The figure uses the bar convention: a
# horizontal line joins two parents and a vertical drop from its midpoint ends
# at the child. Left parent is recorded as sire, right as dam -- the paper
# marks no sexes, and no published value depends on the assignment.
#
#     2 x 3 -> 5           5 x 6 -> 7
#     1 x 2 -> 9           4 x 5 -> 10          7 x 8 -> 11, 12, 13
#
#   founders: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8   (f = 6)
#
# CORROBORATION -- this is not a guessed topology. Appendix A run on it gives
# the raw contributions of Table I "Step 1" EXACTLY:
#
#     animal    1      2      3      4      5      6      7      8
#     Step 1  0.100  0.225  0.125  0.100  0.250  0.150  0.300  0.300
#
# and Appendix B round 2 (after ancestor 7 is selected) reproduces "Step 2":
#
#     animal    1      2      3      4      5      6      8
#     Step 2  0.100  0.150  0.050  0.100  0.100  0.000  0.300
#
# The paper's own narrative check also holds: "the marginal contribution of
# individual 6 is zero because it contributed only through 7" (p.8) -- 6's
# only offspring is 7.
#
# PUBLISHED EXPECTED VALUES
#   marginal contributions, in selection order:
#     7 = 0.300, 8 = 0.300, 2 = 0.150, 1 = 0.100, 4 = 0.100, 5 = 0.050, 3 = 0.000
#   they sum to 1.000 (Table I "Total")
#   implied f_a = 1 / 0.225 = 4.44
#   NOTE the round-1 tie: 7 and 8 both hold 0.300 and the paper selects 7.
#   That is one INSTANCE, not a stated rule -- the paper declines to specify a
#   tie-break (p.10). PyPedal uses the lowest ID.
#
# GENERATIONS are labels designating the reference population, not biological
# depth: 1 = the eight numbered ancestors, 2 = the population under study.
# The effective-ancestor routines require generations to be defined.
#
# pedformat: asdg
# Columns are:
#    Animal Sire Dam Generation
1 0 0 1
2 0 0 1
3 0 0 1
4 0 0 1
5 2 3 1
6 0 0 1
7 5 6 1
8 0 0 1
9 1 2 2
10 4 5 2
11 7 8 2
12 7 8 2
13 7 8 2
